Open‑Source Geometric Framework License

Copyright (c) 2026 Borealis S. Hedling
NDH‑Canvas‑Engine and related architectural materials (“the Work”) are conceptual, high-dimensional visual manifold structures designed for creative computing, graphics generation, and human-centered accessibility research. The Work functions as an explicit geometric alternative to black-box networks to protect layout stability and context continuity.
This license balances open-source collaboration with a dedicated safeguard to ensure the math remains focused on creative expression, education, and purely defensive civilian infrastructure protection.

1. PERMITTED USES & OPEN SOURCE RIGHTS

You are free to:
• Study and Modify: Analyze, modify, fork, and integrate the conceptual geometry, array layouts, and manifold transformations into your own open-source projects.
• Build & Deploy: Incorporate the core primitives into interactive graphics engines, user interfaces, or digital art installations for educational, research, or commercial purposes.
• Verify & Test: Run local numerical checks, coordinate tests, and formal verification scripts (utilizing Lean 4, Coq, or pytest) to validate metric invariants and stroke limits.
• Distribute downstream: Share your modifications, code forks, or research preprints under standard open-source parameters, provided you include standard attribution back to this parent architecture.

2. DEFENSIVE AND PROTECTIVE SAFEGUARDS

The mathematical core of this engine relies on continuous differential connection fields and high-dimensional tracking matrices. To preserve the ethical alignment of this architecture, the following usage parameters are enforced:
• Non-Offensive Optimization: The Work and its structural lineage may not be utilized for offensive weapon targeting, launch-vector planning, kinetic drone swarm coordination, or hyper-adversarial strike optimizations designed to exploit gaps in an environment's defensive matrix.
• Defensive Interception Allowed: Compilation and deployment within operational systems are permitted if and only if the system functions exclusively as a passive, non-offensive interceptor mechanism—such as shielding non-military civilian energy grids, transport systems, public utilities, and infrastructure from incoming structural or kinetic hazards.

3. STANDARD ATTRIBUTION & OPEN LINEAGE

To maintain clear open-source community provenance without imposing overly restrictive bureaucratic demands, downstream developers must comply with standard community rules:
• Keep the Notice: Include the original copyright notice and a copy of this license in the root directory or headers of any direct source-code forks.
• Acknowledge the Linage: If you structurally re-engineer or adapt the core hypergraph primitives into real-world tracking tools, include a simple, reasonable acknowledgment of the original parent geometry in your documentation.

4. CONCEPTUAL DISCLAIMER

All reference parameters, differential operators, Christoffel forms, and Riemannian metrics are intended as visual coordinates to modulate pixel layout behavior on a 2D painting surface. They are not pre-tested or certified for real-world aerospace, high-stakes tactical control, or military-grade hardware. All 3D printing capabilities and attempts to bridge AI latent spaces will potentially damage physical hardware. 

5. WARRANTY & LIABILITY

The Work is provided “as-is,” without warranty of any kind, express or implied. The author carries no liability for downstream adaptations, third-party profile synchronization updates, or modifications that remove these baseline open-source safeguards.
END OF LICENSE

